; Minimal, self-contained GROMACS-format topology for a np>1 (MPI cross-rank
; rigid-body migration) verification test. No bonded terms are needed: the
; only thing under test is whether a 3-atom rigid body correctly migrates
; from one MPI domain to another as its center of mass crosses the domain
; boundary along x, pushed there by LJ repulsion from a nearby "pusher" atom
; (deterministic: initial velocities are all zero, so no RNG dependency).
;
; Units are native GROMACS (nm, kJ/mol); GENESIS converts internally to its
; own units (Angstrom, kcal/mol).

[ defaults ]
; nbfunc  comb-rule  gen-pairs  fudgeLJ  fudgeQQ
1         2          no         1.0      1.0

; RA's sigma is deliberately tiny: spdyn does not honor this file's
; [exclusions] section (confirmed at runtime: "has [exclusions] list in
; grotop, but it is not used in spdyn"), and GENESIS's [RIGIDBODY] feature
; itself does not exclude intra-body nonbonded interactions either (see
; tests/rigid-body/SPEC.md) -- so the 3 rigid-body atoms, ~0.6-0.8 A apart,
; would otherwise repel each other with an enormous, physically
; meaningless LJ force. With sigma_RA this small, the Lorentz-Berthelot
; combination sigma_RA-RA = sigma_RA stays far below the actual intra-body
; separation (negligible self-interaction), while sigma_RA-BG =
; (sigma_RA+sigma_BG)/2 stays large enough to give a real repulsive push
; from the separate "pusher" (BG) atom a few Angstrom away.
[ atomtypes ]
; name    mass      charge   ptype  sigma    epsilon
RA        12.0000   0.0000   A      0.0500   1.5000
BG        12.0000   0.0000   A      0.6500   1.5000

[ moleculetype ]
; name  nrexcl
RIG     1

[ atoms ]
; nr  type  resnr  residue  atom  cgnr  charge
1     RA    1      RIG      A1    1     0.0
2     RA    1      RIG      A2    1     0.0
3     RA    1      RIG      A3    1     0.0

[ moleculetype ]
; name  nrexcl
BGM     1

[ atoms ]
; nr  type  resnr  residue  atom  cgnr  charge
1     BG    1      BGM      B1    1     0.0

[ system ]
np2 rigidbody migration test

[ molecules ]
; Compound   #mols
RIG          1
BGM          3
